WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:17.070
Hi, this is Dr. Jelena Trajkovic, CECS Department, Cal State Long Beach. Today we start a new chapter, and this new chapter is about combinational, standard combinational data path components.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:33.220
So we are going to start working with maxes. Maxes are short for multiplexer. So a multiplexer is a combinational circuit.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:47.580
Remember, combinational means that there are just gates inside the black box and whatever

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.740
is on the input is going to influence output by means of propagating through those gates

00:00:54.540 --> 00:01:02.220
and by the function that those gates are performed. So multiplexer is such a circuit that it has

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:11.060
multiple inputs and we are going to separate. We are going to call some inputs multiple data inputs

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:22.060
and then it has some control, control is the nature of it, and they are going to be called

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:38.140
select. To be precise, in terms of multiplexer, you can have 2 to the power of n, that is

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:47.660
not a nice tool, 2 to the power of n different data inputs. This n here is going to be number

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:55.580
select inputs. So these are all inputs and they are going to produce one and

00:01:55.580 --> 00:02:07.540
only one output. We're not going to put output plural here. Usually when we

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:13.260
start talking about multiplexers we are going to call them by number of data

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:28.160
inputs so basically 2 to the n to 1 max. What is my only question? It is that we

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:34.720
have multiple inputs I'm going to do only two because our example is going to

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:42.600
be 2 to 1 max. You have 41 max in the book so that's why I'm giving you a

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.640
a different one in this mini lecture.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.580
So we have two inputs.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.840
Think about these inputs like multiple train tracks

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.280
that are coming into the station.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.920
And we have fewer train station platforms

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.720
than we have two train tracks.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.980
So suppose that this is a platform,

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.680
that platform is going to be similar to our output.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:16.780
and then we have these inputs which are going to be our data I'm going to put

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:23.720
call them data in so these are those two. We need to have a mechanism to select

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:36.160
are we going to pass train from this track to the platform or we will

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:47.080
pass train from this train track to the app and we have to have a mechanism to

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:54.120
move the decision between those things and that is the function that our

00:03:54.120 --> 00:04:01.520
control input which is called select is going to perform so multiplexer is

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:11.120
nothing else but a selector. So speaking of multiplexer, let's look into this

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:24.360
example of 221max. Let's look first into block diagram. Block diagram is

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:31.080
kind of black box approach. It's not really, I mean, you don't see how are

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:36.600
things done inside, but you have to know what are the functions that are being

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:45.240
made inside. So we have input 0 and input 1. It's very very important that you call

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:55.590
them with indices 0 and 1 or 0, 1, 2, 3 or so and so forth. And we have one bit

00:04:55.590 --> 00:05:01.090
that is connected to input 0 and one bit that is connected to input 1. We have

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:05.470
this control signal which is going to call select and you're going to call it

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:15.560
S0 that is connected to S inputs and then we have output which is Y. So

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:24.160
because this is a small circuit I could say okay I have total of all possible

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:31.080
inputs are 3, 2 data and 1 control and I'm going to say hey I have S0 and I

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:36.080
I have I1 and I2, and I'm going to make truth table

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.440
in terms of Y.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:42.360
However, when we go beyond two to one multiplexer,

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.860
that representation is becoming useless.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.880
So I'm going to teach you immediately the representation

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.780
that is good for all the maxis.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:55.960
We are going to put just select signals here

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.960
on the left-hand side as our inputs.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:05.640
and on the right-hand side you're going to put out. Select signal can have,

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:15.160
because it's just one bit, it can have two inputs, sorry, two values of inputs,

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:23.800
0 and 1. When select is equal to 0, so I would like highlighter, when select is

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:36.240
equal to zero, we are going to connect input zero to Y and our output is going

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:48.160
to be our output is going to be I0. Why am I not putting zero or one on the

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:55.320
right-hand side, one side of I? I'm not putting it there because I don't know

00:06:55.320 --> 00:07:00.480
what is connected to I0. So whatever is connected to I0 that is going to be

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:10.080
quote-unquote forwarded to Y. If the output, let's go to opposite color, if the

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:19.600
control signal, select signal or control input is 1, we are going to

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:28.080
forget this purple line and we are going to connect, we are going to connect

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:44.670
whatever is in input 1, we are going to connect it to output. And that is how

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:53.420
multiplexer works. We will proceed to equations and circuits in the next video.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:55.900
Thank you.

